<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pepi I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">23rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/23rd-century-bce">23rd century BCE</a> · Also known as Pepi I Meryre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pepi I Meryre was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixth-dynasty-of-egypt">Sixth Dynasty of Egypt</a> whose long reign was one of the most active of the Old Kingdom. He built widely across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, sent military expeditions into the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> under the official Weni and kept up trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byblos">Byblos</a>, where stone vessels bearing his name were dedicated in the temples. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">Copper</a> statues of him found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nekhen">Hierakonpolis</a> are among the earliest large metal sculptures known.</p></div>
